WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:01.500
- Just to set your expectations:

00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:03.360
I'm not jumping from that tower today.

00:00:03.360 --> 00:00:05.640
And I'm not jumping
from that tower either.

00:00:05.640 --> 00:00:06.480
I am going up there

00:00:06.480 --> 00:00:07.980
and, frankly, I've seen the
route I've got to take,

00:00:07.980 --> 00:00:09.180
it looks terrifying enough.

00:00:09.180 --> 00:00:11.940
But that 20 meter platform
is twice the height

00:00:11.940 --> 00:00:13.950
of the tallest Olympic standard board.

00:00:13.950 --> 00:00:14.970
If I jump from up there,

00:00:14.970 --> 00:00:17.400
I'd hit the water at about
70 kilometers an hour.

00:00:17.400 --> 00:00:19.050
That's easy enough speed
that, with no training,

00:00:19.050 --> 00:00:20.400
I would be in hospital.

00:00:20.400 --> 00:00:23.040
I've even got to be harnessed in
while I'm up there just in case.

00:00:23.040 --> 00:00:25.710
But that doesn't apply to Lysanne Richard,

00:00:25.710 --> 00:00:28.080
world class high diver
and cliff diver who is

00:00:28.080 --> 00:00:29.520
going to show me the way up

00:00:29.520 --> 00:00:31.500
and then take the quick route down.

00:00:31.500 --> 00:00:33.090
And down here, safely at pool level,

00:00:33.090 --> 00:00:35.370
someone from the
Montreal Olympic Park's team

00:00:35.370 --> 00:00:38.610
is going to explain why they
built a board that high.

00:00:38.610 --> 00:00:41.370
- It's the biggest
aquatic center in Canada.

00:00:41.370 --> 00:00:46.560
It's a facility that was built
for the Olympics back in 1976

00:00:46.560 --> 00:00:51.450
and it's also right now home
of Team Canada in many sports.

00:00:51.450 --> 00:00:53.130
It's also open to the public.

00:00:53.130 --> 00:00:54.000
- How long have you been training

00:00:54.000 --> 00:00:55.410
to be able to do this sort of thing?

00:00:55.410 --> 00:00:59.370
- I did gymnastic and
diving and circus before,

00:00:59.370 --> 00:01:03.720
but it's been already
22 years that I'm a high diver.

00:01:03.720 --> 00:01:05.390
- And you were in Cirque du Soleil right?

00:01:05.390 --> 00:01:06.810
- Yes. I worked at Cirque
du Soleil for a while,

00:01:06.810 --> 00:01:09.330
but I never did diving
with Cirque du Soleil.

00:01:09.330 --> 00:01:10.163
- Okay.

00:01:10.163 --> 00:01:13.007
- It was completely renovated in 2015.

00:01:13.007 --> 00:01:16.950
Lysanne was well aware
of the Olympic Center.

00:01:16.950 --> 00:01:19.230
She was also training here.

00:01:19.230 --> 00:01:21.420
So when we renovated,

00:01:21.420 --> 00:01:24.390
she looked at all the
space here and she said

00:01:24.390 --> 00:01:27.660
maybe you could put a high
diving platform there.

00:01:27.660 --> 00:01:30.540
And we started with a 18 meter platform.

00:01:30.540 --> 00:01:33.180
Then two years later she said,
well, you know,

00:01:33.180 --> 00:01:37.050
I think you guys got room
for a 20 meter platform.

00:01:37.050 --> 00:01:39.450
So we built a 20 meter platform,

00:01:39.450 --> 00:01:43.260
and we became the only
place in North America

00:01:43.260 --> 00:01:48.260
where people can perform high
diving in an interior space.

00:01:48.390 --> 00:01:51.060
Winter can be harsh sometime,

00:01:51.060 --> 00:01:55.590
but because we have this facility,
they can train all year long.

00:01:55.590 --> 00:01:58.890
- So how do you learn to do this?

00:01:58.890 --> 00:02:02.070
do you just, like, work up
from lower heights and-

00:02:02.070 --> 00:02:05.730
- Yeah! You do not do high
diving if somebody asks you.

00:02:05.730 --> 00:02:06.563
- Right.

00:02:06.563 --> 00:02:09.810
- Like, you really have to feel that
you have to do it, you know?

00:02:09.810 --> 00:02:10.860
So just right here.

00:02:10.860 --> 00:02:12.130
- Okay. Up the ladder.

00:02:12.130 --> 00:02:15.540
Oh, I can feel the positive
pressure, the heat...

00:02:15.540 --> 00:02:17.010
There's air coming up through here!

00:02:17.010 --> 00:02:23.701
- Yeah, so this is the last chance of
changing your mind!

00:02:23.701 --> 00:02:25.391
- Yeah, no, it's fine.

00:02:25.391 --> 00:02:27.270
I'm going to be harnessed in.
It's okay.

00:02:27.270 --> 00:02:28.530
- Yeah

00:02:28.530 --> 00:02:29.363
- Let's go.

00:02:29.363 --> 00:02:33.810
- The structure that is here
was built initially

00:02:33.810 --> 00:02:38.010
because people needed to have
access to change the lights.

00:02:38.010 --> 00:02:41.160
The 12 and the 15 meters is attached

00:02:41.160 --> 00:02:43.590
to the platform that we have right here.

00:02:43.590 --> 00:02:46.620
But the 20 meter is
attached through the roof.

00:02:46.620 --> 00:02:49.920
- I've got to be harnessed in
up here with a lot of stuff.

00:02:49.920 --> 00:02:51.990
You just have a safety loop.

00:02:51.990 --> 00:02:53.130
- Because I'm an acrobat,

00:02:53.130 --> 00:02:56.070
I have the authorization to
go only with the hand loop.

00:02:56.070 --> 00:02:58.051
- Right. Let's go.

00:02:58.051 --> 00:02:59.310
Oh, this platform bounces!

00:03:01.770 --> 00:03:04.378
- Yes. Because it bends, it's not
going to break. All right!

00:03:04.378 --> 00:03:07.878
- Yeah. You are 15 meters up
from the floor.

00:03:07.878 --> 00:03:09.094
- Okay. Lead the way.

00:03:09.094 --> 00:03:12.930
So how many times a day can you do this?
'Cause it's got to be a physical strain.

00:03:12.930 --> 00:03:17.160
- Yeah. I do more of the complementary
training than high diving.

00:03:17.160 --> 00:03:18.330
'Cause I'm 41.

00:03:18.330 --> 00:03:21.147
At one point I had
enough impact on my body,

00:03:21.147 --> 00:03:23.490
so now I train everywhere else

00:03:23.490 --> 00:03:25.680
and I do high diving to perform.

00:03:25.680 --> 00:03:28.470
Depending of your age, of your injury,

00:03:28.470 --> 00:03:31.883
you can go a maximum
six times, by day.

00:03:31.883 --> 00:03:32.716
- Okay.

00:03:32.716 --> 00:03:36.150
- But you cannot do every day
and you cannot high dive every month.

00:03:36.150 --> 00:03:37.590
- It's that much strain on your body.

00:03:37.590 --> 00:03:39.270
- Yeah, because after high diving

00:03:39.270 --> 00:03:41.490
you need a recovery time, you know.

00:03:41.490 --> 00:03:42.990
- Because you're hitting
the water at what,

00:03:42.990 --> 00:03:44.940
70 kilometers an hour,
something like that?

00:03:44.940 --> 00:03:48.300
- Exactly. But in some of my
challenges, I go 27 meters,

00:03:48.300 --> 00:03:50.513
so it's pretty fast.

00:03:50.513 --> 00:03:53.430
And here, the water is warm,
so it's easier on the body.

00:03:53.430 --> 00:03:55.920
But when we go outside or in competition-

00:03:55.920 --> 00:03:58.560
- Oh you might be cliff diving
into cold ocean?

00:03:58.560 --> 00:03:59.393
- Yeah, yeah.

00:03:59.393 --> 00:04:04.680
- We know that FINA, which is the
Federation of Aquatic Sports,

00:04:04.680 --> 00:04:10.470
are working towards having
this sport in the Olympics.

00:04:10.470 --> 00:04:13.680
So we said, well, we might
as well have the equipment.

00:04:13.680 --> 00:04:16.350
We also did the same
thing with skateboarding.

00:04:16.350 --> 00:04:18.330
We also have a big bowl.

00:04:18.330 --> 00:04:21.600
So the goal here is to say after 45 years,

00:04:21.600 --> 00:04:25.350
how can we be in the game,
and be also a place,

00:04:25.350 --> 00:04:29.130
where athletes still
come train 45 years later.

00:04:29.130 --> 00:04:30.510
- This is the 15 meter!

00:04:30.510 --> 00:04:33.598
- This is brand new,
now we have 15,

00:04:33.598 --> 00:04:36.060
to build up the next
high diving generation.

00:04:36.060 --> 00:04:36.893
- Wow.

00:04:36.893 --> 00:04:40.140
- So there's the 10, 12, 15, 18 and 20,

00:04:40.140 --> 00:04:42.060
it makes it really safe,

00:04:42.060 --> 00:04:45.090
because they do not learn
too fast and have accidents.

00:04:45.090 --> 00:04:47.790
- Olympic Games last only two weeks.

00:04:47.790 --> 00:04:49.770
So what's happening when you pay

00:04:49.770 --> 00:04:53.130
more than a billion dollars
for Olympic facilities?

00:04:53.130 --> 00:04:55.410
You need to think about the future.

00:04:55.410 --> 00:04:56.243
- You have a zip wire!

00:04:56.243 --> 00:04:58.230
- Yes. A zip line for this,

00:04:58.230 --> 00:05:00.933
and I also always put
the shoes down, I can-

00:05:05.130 --> 00:05:06.810
- And that's just fun,
that is, that's-

00:05:06.810 --> 00:05:08.716
- I'm always jealous of my shoes.

00:05:08.716 --> 00:05:10.696
I would like to go "aaagh"!

00:05:10.696 --> 00:05:14.340
- We are able to be a place
where they can practice

00:05:14.340 --> 00:05:19.020
but we can also host some
competition, which is quite nice

00:05:19.020 --> 00:05:22.830
for a facility that was built 46 years ago.

00:05:22.830 --> 00:05:25.740
- This is the one bit
where I'm not harnessed in.

00:05:25.740 --> 00:05:27.000
- Yeah.

00:05:27.000 --> 00:05:28.320
- Okay. There we go.

00:05:28.320 --> 00:05:29.949
You're entirely unharnessed

00:05:29.949 --> 00:05:30.827
- Mm hmm.

00:05:30.827 --> 00:05:32.493
- And I've got twintails on.
All right.

00:05:32.493 --> 00:05:35.196
- But you know, when we dive
it's better to be unharnessed!

00:05:35.196 --> 00:05:36.350
- Yeah, yeah it is!

00:05:36.350 --> 00:05:39.060
Okay. I guess that's the one
question I haven't asked,

00:05:39.060 --> 00:05:43.010
which is "why". Why did you
choose to take this up?

00:05:43.010 --> 00:05:44.910
- At the beginning I wanted to do it

00:05:44.910 --> 00:05:48.150
because I felt brave and I
wanted to be one of the men.

00:05:48.150 --> 00:05:49.440
'Cause at the beginning,

00:05:49.440 --> 00:05:51.750
no women were doing this sport, you know?

00:05:51.750 --> 00:05:55.020
So I wanted to prove that
women, we can make it.

00:05:55.020 --> 00:05:57.240
Then at one point I wanted to do it to

00:05:57.240 --> 00:06:00.387
help the sport progress
and go to the Olympics,

00:06:00.387 --> 00:06:04.350
and help to build, to have the
next generation and to win.

00:06:04.350 --> 00:06:07.800
But now I do not need to compete anymore.

00:06:07.800 --> 00:06:10.410
I want to inspirate the people

00:06:10.410 --> 00:06:13.170
being involved into
the progress of the sport.

00:06:13.170 --> 00:06:17.100
I'm totally in the present moment
when I do high dive,

00:06:17.100 --> 00:06:20.400
and I'm a mom, I have three kids,
I have a lot of jobs.

00:06:20.400 --> 00:06:24.099
When I high dive
there is nothing,

00:06:24.099 --> 00:06:26.850
no grocery list, nothing.

00:06:26.850 --> 00:06:28.910
- So I now just duck under here.

00:06:28.910 --> 00:06:31.410
Agh. I'm harnessed in, I'm harnessed in.

00:06:31.410 --> 00:06:32.805
I'm harnessed in.

00:06:32.805 --> 00:06:37.860
I'm harnessed in...
I've got two separate harness points.

00:06:37.860 --> 00:06:38.700
All right.

00:06:38.700 --> 00:06:42.600
- This is where champions
are built, right here,

00:06:42.600 --> 00:06:47.600
in those facilities, which are
also accessible to everybody.

00:06:48.360 --> 00:06:50.070
- (low voice) I don't want to
distract her at this point

00:06:50.070 --> 00:06:53.163
but when you're up here,
you do realize that is...

00:06:54.000 --> 00:06:55.400
that's a very long way down.

00:07:03.913 --> 00:07:05.820
[cheering]
Woo!

00:07:05.820 --> 00:07:08.403
I'd applaud, but my hands are a bit busy.

00:07:22.740 --> 00:07:26.073
Right, I'm going to take the
slow route down, it's safer.

